{"data":{"attachmentkeynames":["rs"],"desc":"Advances ONE accepted/in-progress kb.plan item by REASONING about it via agent.llm.tool_loop, and CLOSES the loop on completion. The human move_item to `accepted` is the authorization; the item's claim + FULL detail (never truncated - the 3000-char cap was removed 2026-10 so the whole plan rides every step prompt) is the GOAL. HUMAN NOTES (agent.plan.add_note, the kanban card's note form): every note on the entry rides the step prompt in full, under 'HUMAN NOTES' (they outrank detail and prior steps where they conflict); notes the loop has not consumed yet (no seen_at) are listed first as 'NEW since your last step', and the post-turn write stamps seen_at on exactly the notes that prompt presented, only when the turn reached the model - so a note typed mid-turn, or shown to a failed turn, stays NEW for the next step. step_log entries record notes_presented/notes_new; the result carries notes_new. Gate: only accepted/in-progress entries are steppable (a `blocked` item is refused until a human moves it back to accepted). START TRANSITION: an `accepted` item is moved to `in-progress` in its own journaled, base-hashed write BEFORE the tool_loop turn runs (label 'plan started (in-progress)'), so the kanban board shows the agent is working on it for the whole turn; if that write fails (stale_base) it returns action start_failed and the turn is NOT run (moved_to_in_progress=true in the result when it happened). FRESH BASE: after the turn the board is re-read and the entry re-located by claim, so the step_log/latest write lands on current state under the current hash (still base-hashed - never forced); a DONE only auto-completes an item still in accepted/in-progress (a human's mid-turn move wins). BLOCKED TRANSITION: a turn ending STATUS: BLOCKED (the agent needs a human - decision, access, external dependency) moves the item to the `blocked` lifecycle (the kanban's blocked column) in the SAME atomic post-turn write (label 'plan blocked (needs a human)', moved_to_blocked=true), only if it is still in accepted/in-progress; the blocker text stays on the card's `latest` and in step_log. Blocked items are neither steppable nor eligible for the plan worker, so the loop goes on to the next unblocked task instead of spending turns re-proving the blocker. SUB-ITEMS: an entry other items point to via `parent` is a container - it refuses to step while any child is unfinished (children_open, a blocked child counts as unfinished), so the loop drives the children; when the item that completes is a child and was the last unfinished sibling, its parent is marked `completed` in the SAME atomic journaled write (rolled_up_parent), so a parent is done only when all children are done. CONVERGENCE GUARD: prior steps = step_log length; at/over MAX_PLAN_STEPS it refuses with needs_reapproval until re-accepted. DONE requires a VERIFIED: evidence line or tool_loop parses it as IN_PROGRESS. The bounded final answer is journaled to step_log via patch_control_facet - on stale_base it aborts, never forces. base is the board hash from agent.plan.board (empty skips the initial check). Returns action stepped|completed|blocked|step_failed|start_failed|needs_reapproval|defer_stale|gated, loop_status, moved_to_in_progress, moved_to_blocked, steps_taken/max_steps, rolled_up_parent, notes_new.","import":"use ndata::dataobject::DataObject;\nuse ndata::dataarray::DataArray;\nuse ndata::data::Data;","params":[{"name":"claim","type":"String"},{"name":"base","type":"String"},{"name":"nn_sessionid","type":"String"}],"returntype":"FLAT","type":"rust"},"id":"opjijl1a158e0142bq1bd6","readers":[],"time":1792758475352,"username":"system","writers":[]}